 workspace hash for cross‑machine import.\n\nIntended outcome: a mergeable branch that lets a user portably export a Cursor agent session to a `.cursor-chat.json` archive on machine A and import it on machine B (different repo path, different machine), and that also silently attaches the archive to committed checkpoints so `entire` history carries it.\n\n## Approach\n\n### Phase 0 — Rebase + build baseline\n\n1. `git fetch origin && git rebase origin/main` on `cursor-export-import-sessions`.\n2. Resolve Agent‑interface drift (main has evolved — e.g., the CLAUDE.md banner now lists only claude-code/gemini/opencode/cursor; some agents were removed and `docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md` updated). Re‑verify:\n   - `agent.CheckpointContributor` interface still compiles where defined (`cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go:173-182` pre‑rebase — move if file was split).\n   - `lifecycle.go:375-381` dispatch still attaches to the turn‑end path.\n   - `strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go` extractor + `checkpoint/committed.go:417-428` tree write still valid.\n3. `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` green before continuing.\n\n### Phase 1 — Harden existing export/import (cursor-agent CLI paths only)\n\nFiles: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/cursor_export.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/cursor_import.go`.\n\n1. **Read‑only SQLite on export.** In `ExportDB` (`chatexport.go:106-154`) open with DSN `file:<path>?mode=ro&immutable=1&_journal_mode=WAL` (via `modernc.org/sqlite` URI form) and drop the `PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(PASSIVE)` write. Safer when Cursor holds the DB. Fall back to `mode=ro` (no `immutable=1`) if the first open errors — `immutable=1` rejects WAL sidecar files.\n2. **Path‑normalized workspace hash.** Add a `WorkspaceMapping{absolute_path, git_root_relative, repo_remote}` block to `ChatArchive`. On export, populate from `paths.WorktreeRoot()` (`cmd/entire/cli/paths`) + `git remote get-url origin` (best effort). On import, if `--workspace-hash` not given: recompute from current `WorktreeRoot()`; log the original absolute path from the archive so the user sees why it remapped. Keep `--workspace-hash` / `--project-slug` overrides.\n3. **Transactional overwrite.** In `importCursorDB` (`cursor_import.go:138-193`), write to `store.db.tmp` + `os.Rename` once the transaction commits. Remove the manual `.db`/`.db-wal`/`.db-shm` delete sequence; rely on rename atomicity. If `--force=false` and target exists, error before opening anything.\n4. **Archive validation.** Reject `Format != \"cursor-chat-export\"` and `Version > 1` with a clear message. Round‑trip one unknown extra field via `json.RawMessage` so future versions don't break today's reader.\n5. **Drop the two `//TODO: why do we not use here subagents dir?`** at `manual_commit_condensation.go:496,544` — either file a follow‑up todo or resolve by threading the tasks dir through. Decide during rebase review; do not leave stale TODOs.\n\n### Phase 2 — New `cursor-sessions` command\n\nFile: `cmd/entire/cli/cursor_sessions.go` (new). Register in `root.go` next to the existing two commands.\n\n- `entire cursor-sessions` — enumerate `~/.cursor/chats/*/` + `~/.cursor/projects/*/agent-transcripts/*.jsonl` (or nested `/*/*.jsonl`), join on agent‑id, print a table: `AGENT-ID | WORKSPACE (from projects slug) | DB SIZE | TRANSCRIPT LINES | LAST MODIFIED`.\n- `--json` flag emits the same list as JSON for scripting.\n- Reuse discovery helpers already in `cursor/chatexport.go` (glob logic) — factor them into an unexported `discoverSession(agentID)` returning `{dbPath, transcriptPath}`, reused by export + sessions list.\n- Follow command‑add pattern in `status.go` (`RunE`, `cmd.OutOrStdout`, `SilenceUsage` for prereqs).\n\n### Phase 3 — Tests\n\n1. **Unit — `cursor/chatexport_test.go`**:\n   - Build a fixture SQLite (`modernc.org/sqlite`) with known `meta` + `blobs` rows and a small JSONL file, call `ExportChatArchive` pointed at a synthesized `~/.cursor` tree under `t.TempDir()`, assert archive round‑trips byte‑for‑byte (base64 blobs decoded back to original bytes).\n   - Read‑only open test: DB that has a WAL sidecar should still export cleanly.\n2. **Unit — `cursor_import_test.go`** (new): roundtrip — export from fixture A, import to tempdir B with `--workspace-hash=XYZ`, open recreated DB, assert row equality. Also assert `--force=false` + existing file returns error without mutating target.\n3. **Integration — `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/cursor_export_test.go`**: build tag `//go:build integration`. Uses `testutil.InitRepo`. Drives the `entire cursor-export` cobra command end‑to‑end with a fake `~/.cursor` tree under `t.TempDir()` and `t.Setenv(\"HOME\", ...)`. Mirrors the `status_test.go` pattern for cobra invocation. No `os.Chdir` before `t.Parallel()`.\n4. **Vogon canary**: the Vogon binary does not use Cursor storage; skip. Cursor export is tested via unit/integration only. Do **not** run real‑agent E2E (costs money) — CLAUDE.md forbids proactive E2E runs.\n\n### Phase 4 — Docs + registration\n\n1. Update `docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md` with a \"CheckpointContributor\" bullet describing the optional interface (Cursor is the reference impl).\n2. Short usage section in `docs/` or `cmd/entire/cli/cursor_export.go` long‑help covering: export → copy file → import flow, `--workspace-hash` override semantics, and that the archive also rides along inside committed checkpoints automatically (no user action).\n3. No changes to `CLAUDE.md` unless rebase demands it.\n\n## Critical files\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport.go` — export core; add read‑only DSN + `WorkspaceMapping` + shared `discoverSession` helper.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/checkpoint.go` — `ContributeCheckpointFiles`; unchanged unless interface moves post‑rebase.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/cursor_export.go` — wire workspace mapping into archive; long‑help text update.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/cursor_import.go` — transactional rename, archive version validation, normalized hash fallback.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/cursor_sessions.go` — **new**, `cursor-sessions` command.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/root.go` — register new command.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport_test.go` — **new** unit tests.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/cursor_import_test.go` — **new** unit tests.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/cursor_export_test.go` — **new** integration test.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go` — re‑verify `extractExtraFilesFromTree` post‑rebase; resolve stale TODOs at 496/544.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go` — confirm `CheckpointContributor` still exported.\n\n## Reusable helpers (already in repo)\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/paths` — `WorktreeRoot()` for repo‑root resolution (not `os.Getwd`; see CLAUDE.md \"Repo Root vs CWD\").\n- `cmd/entire/cli/testutil` — `InitRepo`, `WriteFile`, `GitAdd`, `GitCommit` for git‑touching tests.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent.ChunkJSONL` / `ReassembleJSONL` — if we later need to chunk a fat archive into the metadata branch, reuse these.\n- Cobra pattern in `cmd/entire/cli/status.go` — canonical `RunE` + `cmd.OutOrStdout` example for adding `cursor-sessions`.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` — all green (includes unit + integration + vogon canary per CLAUDE.md).\n2. Manual roundtrip on the dev box:\n   - `cursor-agent` a short session on a throwaway repo to populate `~/.cursor/chats/<hash>/<id>/store.db` + transcript.\n   - `entire cursor-sessions` — confirm the session shows up.\n   - `entire cursor-export <id> /tmp/snap.cursor-chat.json` — file written, report shows meta/blob/transcript counts.\n   - In a different repo path: `entire cursor-import /tmp/snap.cursor-chat.json` (no flags) — confirm new `~/.cursor/chats/<new-hash>/<id>/store.db` created; `cursor-agent --resume <id>` reads it.\n   - Make a commit via Entire while in the first repo; inspect the checkpoint on `entire/checkpoints/v1` and confirm `<id>.cursor-chat.json` rides inside the checkpoint tree (use `git show entire/checkpoints/v1:<shard>/<rest>/0/<id>.cursor-chat.json | jq .format`).\n3. Regression: run with `ACCESSIBLE=1` to confirm no TUI prompts were introduced that skip the accessible path.\n4. Do NOT run real‑agent E2E (CLAUDE.md prohibition). Canary only.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1214,"cache_read_input_tokens":102590,"output_tokens":4531,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1214,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4531,"cache_read_input_tokens":102590,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1214,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1214},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaJdsEy4CJ4VNmd6iu2o7","type":"assistant","uuid":"202b9596-7053-4aa9-a05d-a9212ccb9fbd","timestamp":"2026-04-22T10:17:50.038Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/cursor-export-import-sessions","sessionId":"ce8c32dc-4379-4162-9ca7-f9d7eee44100","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"it-s-been-a-while-cheeky-boot"}
