{"parentUuid":"4ae2d158-ba2c-46c2-b15a-1fdc64386cb8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019XAdK4R26RDx4ZDceBcotz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017YvBw3eGUyEHZYE1jf4YD2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gtrrz-victor/.claude/plans/it-s-been-a-while-cheeky-boot.md","content":"# Plan: Resume Cursor session export/import (cursor-agent CLI)\n\n## Context\n\nBranch `cursor-export-import-sessions` paused Feb 2026 after 2 commits (`15c46863d`, `89b123187`). Already shipped:\n\n- `entire cursor-export <agent-id> [out]` + `entire cursor-import <archive>`\n- Portable archive: `ChatArchive{format,version,agentId,store{meta,blobs},transcript[]}`. SQLite via pure‑Go `modernc.org/sqlite`.\n- `agent.CheckpointContributor` interface + Cursor impl embeds `<sessionID>.cursor-chat.json` into committed checkpoints via `WriteCommittedOptions.ExtraFiles` → `strategy.extractExtraFilesFromTree`.\n\nGaps: no tests, SQLite opened read/write (risks lock when Cursor is running), overwrite isn't atomic, no `sessions list`, cross‑machine import needs manual `--workspace-hash`.\n\n**Scope (decided)**: cursor-agent CLI paths only (`~/.cursor/chats/<hash>/<id>/store.db` + `~/.cursor/projects/<slug>/agent-transcripts/<id>.jsonl`). Keep both standalone CLI commands and checkpoint embedding. Rebase branch on `main` first.\n\n**Principles**: KISS, DRY, TDD. Each phase starts with a failing test. Shared helpers live in one place before the second call site.\n\nOutcome: export on machine A, import on machine B at a different repo path, no manual flags; archive also rides inside committed checkpoints.\n\n## Approach\n\n### Phase 0 — Rebase + green baseline\n\n1. `git fetch origin && git rebase origin/main`. Resolve any `Agent` interface drift (CLAUDE.md now lists fewer agents; `docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md` evolved).\n2. `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` green before writing a single new line.\n\n### Phase 1 — Extract the one shared helper (DRY)\n\nBefore any new feature. Factor the existing path‑discovery logic (currently inline in `chatexport.go:44-91`) into an unexported:\n\n```go\n// agent/cursor/locate.go  (new)\nfunc locateSession(agentID string) (dbPath, transcriptPath string, err error)\n```\n\nUsed by export **and** the new sessions‑list command. One place owns the globbing.\n\n### Phase 2 — TDD: read‑only SQLite + atomic import\n\nFailing tests first (`cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport_test.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/cursor_import_test.go`). Use `modernc.org/sqlite` to build a fixture DB under `t.TempDir()`; synthesize a fake `~/.cursor` tree with `t.Setenv(\"HOME\", tmp)`.\n\nTests (write each as failing, then fix):\n\n1. **Roundtrip equality** — export fixture, import into a second tempdir, reopen DB, assert `meta`+`blobs` rows equal.\n2. **Read‑only export with WAL sidecar** — fixture has `store.db-wal`; `ExportChatArchive` succeeds and does not mutate any file.\n3. **Overwrite refusal without `--force`** — target exists; import errors before touching target bytes.\n4. **Atomic overwrite with `--force`** — target exists; import succeeds; on simulated mid‑write failure (inject error after tmp write, before rename) original target is unchanged.\n\nMinimal code to pass:\n\n- `ExportDB` opens `file:<path>?mode=ro&immutable=1`; fallback to `mode=ro` if `immutable=1` errors. Drop the `PRAGMA wal_checkpoint` write.\n- `importCursorDB` writes to `<target>.tmp` then `os.Rename`; delete the manual `.db`/`.db-wal`/`.db-shm` teardown.\n\nThat's it for this phase. Do **not** add a `WorkspaceMapping` struct, archive version bump, or any other field yet — no test demands it.\n\n### Phase 3 — TDD: cross‑machine import without flags\n\nOne failing test in `cursor_import_test.go`: export from repo A path, import from repo B path without `--workspace-hash`, reopen at the computed destination, assert the DB is readable.\n\nMinimal code:\n\n- Add one string field `OriginPath` to `ChatArchive` (not a struct). Populate on export from `paths.WorktreeRoot()`.\n- On import with no `--workspace-hash`, compute hash from current `paths.WorktreeRoot()`. Log the archive's `OriginPath` → new absolute path remap.\n\nTolerate missing `OriginPath` on older archives — empty string is fine. No version bump needed.\n\n### Phase 4 — TDD: `cursor-sessions` command\n\nFailing test in `cmd/entire/cli/cursor_sessions_test.go`: seed a fake `~/.cursor` tree with two sessions under `t.Setenv(\"HOME\", ...)`, run the cobra command with `--json`, assert both agent‑ids appear with db size + transcript line count.\n\nMinimal code: `cursor_sessions.go` using `locateSession` from Phase 1 for per‑id resolution and a `filepath.Glob` walk for discovery. Registered in `root.go`. Follows `status.go` cobra pattern (`RunE`, `cmd.OutOrStdout`, `SilenceUsage`).\n\nText output is nice but optional — `--json` is what the test pins. Text format can be a follow‑up.\n\n### Phase 5 — Integration test (cobra end‑to‑end)\n\nOne file, `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/cursor_export_test.go` (build tag `//go:build integration`). Uses `testutil.InitRepo`. Drives `NewRootCmd().Execute()` with args `[\"cursor-export\", \"<id>\"]` against a `t.Setenv(\"HOME\", ...)` tree. Validates the on‑disk archive parses.\n\nNo separate integration test for import — Phase 2 unit tests cover the logic; the export integration test proves command wiring works.\n\n## Critical files\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/locate.go` — **new**, shared session discovery.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport.go` — read‑only DSN; call `locateSession`; add `OriginPath`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/cursor_import.go` — atomic rename; default `OriginPath`‑aware workspace hash fallback.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/cursor_sessions.go` — **new** command.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/root.go` — register new command.\n- Tests (all **new**): `agent/cursor/chatexport_test.go`, `cursor_import_test.go`, `cursor_sessions_test.